The match starts. I play well   or at least, I play the same way I always play, which is inconsistently, with bursts of competence between stretches of mediocrity. But the chat's reaction transforms the mediocrity into narrative. When I die, it's not failure   it's adversity. When I clutch, it's not luck   it's a growth arc. The audience is writing a story about me, a story about a shy girl with beautiful eyes who's finding her confidence through gaming, and every round is a chapter.

