Fifteen dollars. From a stranger who clicked because the thumbnail   my eyes, framed by lashes and auburn waves   stopped their scroll. Exactly the way Kira described it. "When a cute face shows up on a thumbnail, people click." Except this isn't my face. Or it is my face, with modifications, seen through a frame that hides the parts that don't perform. It's a curated face. A product face. A face that exists only in the rectangle of the webcam preview, bounded by the crop line that separates who I am from who they think I see.

The stream settles into rhythm. I play, I talk, I react. The eyes do the heavy lifting   every expression is amplified by the lashes and the framing. When I'm concentrating, the eyes narrow and the chat says "focus mode activated." When I'm surprised, the eyes widen and the chat says "the wide eyes 🥺." When I laugh   and VoxMorph processes the laugh into something higher, lighter, more musical   the eyes crinkle and the chat says "her eye smile is the best thing on twitch."

