Even the bad performance is met with warmth. Even failure is cushioned. The audience has committed to the narrative   Ellie is the underdog, the shy girl getting better, the diamond in the rough   and a bad game doesn't break the narrative. It enriches it. It makes the next good game sweeter. It makes the audience feel protective, invested, needed.

On EliPlays, a 5-and-7 game would produce silence. Or DarkSlayer saying "lol trash." Here, it produces twenty messages of encouragement and three people telling me to take care of myself.

Same player. Same game. Same score. Different frame.

